#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:32
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:34
msgid ""
"Returns an `Object` with a `stdout` and `stderr` property for testing "
"either streams. Each property is an `Object`, or `false` if color is not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:36
msgid ""
"The `stdout`/`stderr` objects specifies a level of support for color "
"through a `.level` property and a corresponding flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:38
msgid "`.level = 1` and `.hasBasic = true`: Basic color support (16 colors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:39
msgid "`.level = 2` and `.has256 = true`: 256 color support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:40
msgid "`.level = 3` and `.has16m = true`: Truecolor support (16 million colors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:43
msgid "Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:45
msgid "It obeys the `--color` and `--no-color` CLI flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:47
msgid ""
"Can be overridden by the user with the flags `--color` and `--no-color`. "
"For situations where using `--color` is not possible, add the environment"
" variable `FORCE_COLOR=1` to forcefully enable color or `FORCE_COLOR=0` "
"to forcefully disable. The use of `FORCE_COLOR` overrides all other color"
" support checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/supports-color_readme.md:49
msgid ""
"Explicit 256/Truecolor mode can be enabled using the `--color=256` and "
"`--color=16m` flags, respectively."
msgstr ""

